{%- comment -%}
  FAQ PAGE SECTION — every published FAQ entry, grouped by category.

  Slice 12. README "FAQ / Trust Architecture": centrally managed FAQ content
  with categories such as Group Buys, Pricing & Refunds, Production &
  Delivery, Materials & Stones, Ring Sizing, Custom Jewelry, Warranty &
  Repairs, Returns & Cancellations, Payments, and Shipping & Insurance.

  ============================================================================
  CATEGORIES COME FROM THE CONTENT, NOT FROM THIS FILE
  ============================================================================
  Groups are derived from the `category` field of whatever entries exist.
  An entry filed under a category this file does not list STILL APPEARS —
  a list used as a filter would make such entries silently vanish.

  The approved category ORDER (owner decision 2026-10-25, defect F2) is the
  one thing fixed here, because first-appearance order over Shopify's
  unspecified-order collection rendered a different order in production.
  The list orders; it never filters. See the F2 comment below.

  ============================================================================
  NO CONTENT, NO EMPTY SHELL
  ============================================================================
  With no entries the section renders nothing at all — not a heading over
  blank space, and not "No FAQs yet". A published page showing an empty FAQ
  heading looks broken; a page where the section is absent looks like a page
  that does not have an FAQ on it, which is the truth until entries exist.

  THE ORDERING PROBLEM, STATED. Shopify's `shop.metaobjects` returns entries
  in an unspecified order, and Liquid cannot group without materialising the
  category list first. So: approved categories first, in the approved order;
  then any other category in first-appearance order; then uncategorised —
  O(categories x entries), which is fine for an FAQ.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

{{ 'component-faq.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign all_entries = shop.metaobjects.faq_entry.values
-%}

{%- if all_entries != blank and all_entries.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
    <div class="page-width section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h1 class="carat-faq__page-heading {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
          {{ section.settings.heading | escape }}
        </h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <div class="carat-faq__intro rte">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Distinct categories, in first-appearance order (used for categories outside the approved list). {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign seen_categories = '' -%}
      {%- for entry in all_entries -%}
        {%- assign this_category = entry.category | default: '' -%}
        {%- if this_category != blank -%}
          {%- assign needle = '|' | append: this_category | append: '|' -%}
          {%- unless seen_categories contains needle -%}
            {%- assign seen_categories = seen_categories | append: needle -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        F2 (2026-10-25, owner-approved): CATEGORY ORDER IS FIXED HERE.
        First-appearance order over an unspecified-order collection rendered
        the categories in a different order from the approved copy in
        production. The approved categories render first, in this exact
        order; any OTHER nonblank category still renders afterwards (in
        first-appearance order), so a new category is never silently
        dropped; uncategorised entries render last, as before. Question
        order inside each category stays with `sort_key` (faq-list).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign approved_order = 'Group Buys|Pricing & Refunds|Production & Delivery|Materials & Stones|Ring Sizing|Custom Jewelry|Warranty & Repairs|Returns & Cancellations|Payments|Shipping & Insurance|Contacting us' -%}
      {%- assign approved_needles = '|' | append: approved_order | append: '|' -%}
      {%- assign approved_list = approved_order | split: '|' -%}

      {%- for category in approved_list -%}
        {%- assign bucket = all_entries | where: 'category', category -%}
        {%- if bucket.size > 0 -%}
          {%- render 'faq-list',
            entries: bucket,
            heading: category,
            heading_size: 'h2',
            show_category: false
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- assign category_list = seen_categories | split: '|' -%}
      {%- for category in category_list -%}
        {%- if category != blank -%}
          {%- assign needle = '|' | append: category | append: '|' -%}
          {%- unless approved_needles contains needle -%}
            {%- assign bucket = all_entries | where: 'category', category -%}
            {%- render 'faq-list',
              entries: bucket,
              heading: category,
              heading_size: 'h2',
              show_category: false
            -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        UNCATEGORISED ENTRIES STILL APPEAR. An entry with no category is a
        content mistake, but hiding it would make the mistake invisible —
        staff would see the entry in Admin and never on the page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign uncategorised = all_entries | where: 'category', blank -%}
      {%- if uncategorised.size > 0 -%}
        {%- render 'faq-list',
          entries: uncategorised,
          heading: section.settings.uncategorised_heading,
          heading_size: 'h2',
          show_category: false
        -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows every FAQ entry, grouped by category. Entries are managed in Settings → Custom data → Metaobjects → FAQ entry. Categories come from the entries themselves, so adding a category needs no theme change. If there are no entries, this section renders nothing rather than an empty heading."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Page heading",
      "default": "Frequently asked questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h1", "label": "Large" },
        { "value": "h2", "label": "Medium" }
      ],
      "default": "h1",
      "label": "Heading size"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Introduction",
      "info": "Optional."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "uncategorised_heading",
      "label": "Heading for entries with no category",
      "default": "Other questions",
      "info": "An entry saved without a category still appears, under this heading, so the omission is visible rather than hidden."
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.colors.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_top",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_bottom",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "FAQ"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
